  "description": "NESKAA crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C93 H93 Dy7 O38,7(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.564-3.904 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.20-111.41°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C107H114Dy7N7O38. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
